{"text":"### Logical Deduction\n\nTo understand the difference between a stack and a queue, we must analyze their fundamental operating principles, data access methods, and structural behaviors.\n\n#### 1. Fundamental Principles\n*   **Stack**: Operates on the **LIFO** (Last-In, First-Out) principle. This means the last element added to the collection is the first one to be removed. Imagine a stack of plates; you can only take the top plate off, and you must put a new plate on top.\n*   **Queue**: Operates on the **FIFO** (First-In, First-Out) principle. This","output_ids":[13962,59977,48704,2567,271,1206,3418,279,6463,1881,264,5436,321,264,6951,11,567,1902,22903,836,15346,10042,15694,11,795,2528,5245,11,321,23016,26228,13,271,794,220,16,13,88290,55010,198,9,256,2972,4195,92217,7226,942,383,279,2972,43,25166,332,318,5661,30463,11,5339,81600,8,16988,13,1061,3254,279,1483,2315,3568,310,279,4281,369,279,1118,799,310,381,6747,13,36541,264,5436,314,23702,26,488,628,1132,1831,279,1844,11629,974,11,321,488,1902,2113,264,491,11629,383,1844,13,198,9,256,2972,7315,92217,7226,942,383,279,2972,37,25166,332,318,5170,30463,11,5339,81600,8,16988,13,1061],"meta_info":{"id":"e25402f6f5bf440e9e9756847069c400","finish_reason":{"type":"length","length":128},"prompt_tokens":29,"weight_version":"default","num_retractions":0,"input_token_logprobs":[],"output_token_logprobs":[[-0.7143884897232056,13962,null],[-0.6405277252197266,59977,null],[-0.40027928352355957,48704,null],[-0.0003965306677855551,2567,null],[-0.9696552753448486,271,null],[-0.10073002427816391,1206,null],[-0.03235650807619095,3418,null],[-0.00018082413589581847,279,null],[-0.26219457387924194,6463,null],[-0.0002022777043748647,1881,null],[-0.006436451338231564,264,null],[-0.7879748940467834,5436,null],[-0.0002585315378382802,321,null],[-2.4318398573086597e-05,264,null],[-2.8609820219571702e-05,6951,null],[-0.00021908267808612436,11,null],[-0.0047325980849564075,567,null],[-0.0021291938610374928,1902,null],[-0.7390937805175